{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"While checking whether the post-shutdown finding's release condition could be witnessed directly, I found my saved premise was too generous about who releases the parked caller. The network transport's response wait selects on the transport's own shutdown channel as well as the response channel, so closing that transport releases the waiter; but the in-memory transport's Close does nothing except disconnect its peers and never closes the shutdown channel the transport created, so with that transport there is no release signal at all, and an accepted heartbeat after the node is down is not merely unanswered for a while, it is never answered. The observed receipt is unchanged and still the target of its experiment: the post-shutdown delivery received nothing within the bound while the term stayed put, and the live control was answered successfully and moved the term. What changes is the account of the escape, so I corrected the behaviour entry on its existing id with a changed premise that states exactly what moved, added the two source ranges that settle it - the network transport's response wait and the in-memory transport's Close - and recorded the corrected account as the question's current interpretation over the same receipt rather than rerunning anything, since which close path signals what is a source question. The correction sharpens the finding for one transport family and narrows it for the other without changing its operands: the duty is accepted and then has no completion path, the only difference being whether some transport eventually abandons the waiter with a transport-shutdown error or leaves it parked forever. I kept the three counterweights and the limits, including that the parked caller is the heartbeat path for a peer already gone from the cluster's perspective, so the cluster-level consequence stays a stalled per-peer delivery rather than anything about agreement or commit. The six witnessed findings from earlier turns remain recorded and unaffected.\"}"}}
